drm/omap: s1d1374x, rfbi: bus timings from the controller's clocks

The RFBI bus timings came from the bootloader and were lost when the DSS
was reset at boot (on a real N810 the controller then read as revision
0x00). Set them as Nokia's omapfb did (blizzard_setup_clocks(),
calc_reg_timing(), rfbi_convert_timings()): register access timings for
the controller's input clock (CLKI, the N8x0's 19.2 MHz oscillator),
then, with its PLL locked, for the system clock the PLL makes, at the
first RFBI clock divider they fit. RFBI gets rfbi_get_tick_ps() and
rfbi_set_timings(); the N8x0 DT names the controller's input clock.

